2026-09-16T07:51:29.5624426Z       "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nFixes #16366.\r\n\r\n`jsonable_encoder()` ignores `custom_encoder` when encoding types inside a Pydantic `BaseModel`. Furthermore, when a model contains a custom type with `model_config = ConfigDict(arbitrary_types_allowed=True)`, calling `jsonable_encoder(model, custom_encoder={...})` raises `PydanticSerializationError: Unable to serialize unknown type` because `obj.model_dump(mode=\"json\")` is called before custom encoders can run, and `custom_encoder` is not passed to the recursive `jsonable_encoder()` call.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n\r\n- Use `mode=\"python\"` when `custom_encoder` is provided (preserving `mode=\"json\"` for the default/fast path when no `custom_encoder` is passed).\r\n- Pass `custom_encoder=custom_encoder` to the recursive `jsonable_encoder()` call on the dumped model dictionary.\r\n- Add regression test `test_custom_encoders_model` covering custom arbitrary types, standard types (`datetime`), and nested models.",
2026-09-16T07:51:29.5629830Z       "changed_files": 2,
2026-09-16T07:51:29.5630309Z       "closed_at": null,
2026-09-16T07:51:29.5630774Z       "comments": 0,
